  "subtitle": "Io, tu, lui, lei, Lei, noi, voi, loro. The verb ending already shows the person, so Italian often drops the pronoun: Abito a Milano. Use tu with friends and Lei (with a capital L) to be polite.",
  "briefMarks": ["io", "tu", "lui", "lei", "Lei", "noi", "voi", "loro"],
